## Supabase API Patterns

- Client: [shared/api/supabase.js](mdc:src/shared/api/supabase.js)
- Table names: [shared/constants/db.js](mdc:src/shared/constants/db.js)
- Response shaping: [shared/api/db.js](mdc:src/shared/api/db.js) `parseApiResponse`
- Query keys: [shared/constants/queryKeys.ts](mdc:src/shared/constants/queryKeys.ts)
- Transformers map snake_case ↔ camelCase

### Services Layer

Migrated features use a three-layer `services/` structure:

```
features/{feature}/services/
├── apis/index.js          # Raw Supabase calls (async functions)
├── mutations/index.ts     # useMutation hooks (write operations + cache updates)
└── queries/index.ts       # useQuery hooks (read operations)
```

### Feature APIs

| Feature | Location | Pattern |
|---------|----------|---------|
| Pomodoro | [services/apis](mdc:src/features/pomodoro/services/apis/index.js) | `services/` |
| Journals | [services/apis](mdc:src/features/journals/services/apis/index.js) | `services/` |
| Settings | [services/apis](mdc:src/features/settings/services/apis/index.js) | `services/` |
| Auth | [api/auth.js](mdc:src/features/auth/api/auth.js) | Legacy `api/` |

### API Conventions (`services/apis/`)

- Validate `userId` on mutating calls; return `{ error: "User authentication required" }` if missing.
- Transform payloads to DB shape via transformers before insert/update.
- Post-process responses via `parseApiResponse`, then transform back to camelCase.
- Use explicit `.select()` after inserts/updates when you need returned rows.
- Naming: `fetchX`, `createX`, `updateX`, `deleteX`, `getX`, `upsertX`, `sortX`

### Query Conventions (`services/queries/`)

- Use `useQuery` from `@tanstack/react-query`.
- Query keys from `@/shared/constants/queryKeys` — e.g. `queryKeys.tasks.all(userId)`.
- Guard with `enabled: !!userId` to avoid unauthenticated fetches.
- `queryFn` calls the corresponding function from `services/apis/`.

### Mutation Conventions (`services/mutations/`)

- Use `useMutation` from `@tanstack/react-query`.
- `mutationFn` calls the corresponding function from `services/apis/`.
- Update cache in `onSuccess` via `queryClient.setQueryData(queryKeys.X.all(userId), ...)`.
- Use `upsertById` / `deleteById` from `@/shared/utils/jsUtils` for cache array updates.
- Use `onMutate` / `onError` for optimistic updates with rollback where needed.
